.pdxdoc-format-notes This file is consumed by the `doc` tool
  (github.com/paideia-os/doc). Sections are blank-line-separated.
  Section headers are ALL-CAPS on a line by themselves. Bullets are
  hyphen-prefixed. Cross-references use the `see:<tool>` marker,
  parsed by doc.M3+ into hyperlink records. See
  design/release-1.0.md §7 for the format rationale.

NAME

pkg -- paideia-os package manager. Installs, removes, lists, and
audits signed tool packages; the tool that bootstraps every other
tool in the R49/R50 waves. (There is no `upgrade` subcommand at
1.0.0 -- tracked as open issue #23, not yet landed.)

SYNOPSIS

pkg <subcommand> [<arguments>]

Subcommands recognised by `Dispatch::dispatch_subcommand` (exact
byte-compare on five names with distinct first bytes):
- install <name>                 -- install a signed package
- remove  <name>                 -- remove an installed package (undo-journalled)
- list                           -- list installed packages
- verify  <name>                 -- re-verify an installed package's signatures (stub at 1.0.0)
- keys                           -- show the trusted signing keys (stub at 1.0.0)

pkg --help                       -- print usage + one line per subcommand
pkg --version                    -- print "pkg 1.0.0"

--help and --version are wired at the top level (ENH-006 #31): they
short-circuit before subcommand dispatch and work with or without a
subcommand or positional argument present. No other flag has a body
wired at 1.0.0.

--dry-run, --json and --schema are recognised by libpdx-argv's parser
(they parse cleanly) but have no body -- passing them today has no
observable effect. --dry-run is tracked as ENH-007 (#32); --json /
--schema stay reserved-and-unwired until `list` / `install` emit live
records rather than one demo record per run. No other flag exists in
this tool's vocabulary: `--verbose`, `--quiet`, `--color=`, and
`--no-cap:<name>` were never real (see design/argv-surface.md §4).

DESCRIPTION

pkg is the R49-wave package manager: the tool that installs every
other tool in the paideia-os tooling ecosystem, and the one that
bootstraps itself (`pkg install pkg` against a from-source build).

**Dual-signed manifests.** Every package ships a `manifest.pdxsig`
whose 64-byte header reserves two separate public-key lengths (author
+ paideia-root) and whose signature block is exactly
2 x (4B length + signature), both ML-DSA-65 over `header || body`.
`mc_verify_signatures` verifies author then root, then cross-checks
the manifest's `ROOT_FPR` tag against the machine-local fingerprint at
/system/keys/paideia_root_pk.fpr. A compromised author key does not
compromise the mirror. Verification is all-or-nothing.

At 1.0.0 this verification has never actually run: `mc_verify_body_hash`
and `mc_verify_signatures` (`src/manifest_codec.pdx`) return unconditional
STUB codes (`MC_HASH_STUB` / `MC_VERIFY_STUB`) pending the paideia-as
ML-DSA-65 verify intrinsic (blocked on paideia-as v0.33-crypto-kdf; the
sign half of that intrinsic landed at paideia-as v0.23.0, but pkg needs
verify, not sign). No signature has ever been checked by this tool.
`install` also has no network-fetch stage at 1.0.0: it reads a fixed
staging path (`_install_staging`, currently zero-init `.bss`) rather
than fetching from a mirror, so it refuses at the header-magic check
before reaching either verify seam.

SUBCOMMANDS

install <name>
  Real pipeline (`src/install.pdx`); refuses at the header stage today
  because `_install_staging` is zero-init and fails the "pdxsig\0\0"
  magic check -- exit 1. Steps, in order: header parse -> body-hash
  verify (STUB) -> signature verify (STUB) -> KindPackageManifest
  mint -> elevate for KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write,/pkgs) (60s window, via
  libpdx-elevate; ENH-008 #33) -> KIND_PDXFS_TXN open -> extract
  (STUB) -> commit. Emits one InstallProgressRecord per stage on the
  semantic pipe (pdxsig.pkg.ipr.v1 schema) and records that schema on
  the audit entry (ENH-012 #37).

remove <name>
  Real pipeline (`src/remove.pdx`); refuses at the lookup stage today
  (`/system/packages/` has no readdir op at this substrate) -- exit 1.
  Since ENH-008 (#33), remove also requests the same bounded-lifetime
  KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write,/pkgs) cap install does, ahead of the lookup
  stage, so it never gains a live unelevated destructive path once the
  readdir gate closes. Writes a `pdxundo` header (real byte layout;
  body-loop lands with the per-file tar walk) so a future `undo pkg
  remove <name>` can reconstruct the install from the trash subtree.
  `--wipe` is not implemented -- stripped from this doc per ENH-002
  (#27); shipping an irreversible trash-shred ahead of the recoverable
  trash path itself inverts the I5 undo obligation.

list
  Real body (`src/list.pdx`); prints a header + a fixed placeholder
  line, exit 0. `pkg_list_enumerate` is a STUB that always returns 0 --
  no live walk of `/system/packages/` exists yet. Emits one demo
  PackageManifest record (name "pkg") on the semantic pipe
  (pdxsig.pkg.pmf.v1 schema) and records that schema on the audit
  entry (ENH-012 #37). `--available` (query a mirror index) is not
  implemented -- stripped from this doc per ENH-002; blocked on the
  readdir gate and superseded by the index-format question open issue
  #20 raises.

verify <name>
  Stub at 1.0.0 (`PkgSubcommandsM1::pkg_verify_stub`): prints
  "pkg verify: body not implemented at M1 (lands at M2)" and exits 3.
  Ignores any positional argument. A real body is the cheapest genuine
  win in this backlog -- no network or elevate needed, the manifest
  already travels with the install -- tracked as ENH-004 (#29).

keys
  Stub at 1.0.0 (`PkgSubcommandsM1::pkg_keys_stub`): prints
  "pkg keys: body not implemented at M1 (lands at M5)" and exits 3.
  Dispatch matches `keys\0` only and ignores any further positional,
  so `pkg keys list` and `pkg keys` are identical today. A real `keys
  list` body needs a `/system/keys/` read authority this tool's
  baseline `caps.decl` does not yet grant -- tracked as ENH-005 (#30).
  `keys add` / `keys remove` are out of scope at any milestone
  (trust-root mutation through the package manager).

CAPS

Baseline (loader-seeded via InitCap sidecar):
- KIND_USER (self)                            -- identity root
- KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)                  -- pipe substrate
- KIND_PDXFS_FILE (read, /system/packages/)   -- package enumeration
- KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL (invoke, svc.elevate-broker)  -- install + remove
                                                        elevate flow

Per-operation (acquired via libpdx-elevate for a 60s window, both
`install` and `remove` since ENH-008 #33):
- KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, /pkgs)              -- install/remove destination

The elevate mask requests bit 0 only (`PE_CAP_MASK_PDXFS_WRITE_PKGS =
0x01`). It does **not** also acquire KIND_NETWORK or KIND_SIGNATURE in
the same window -- an earlier draft of this document claimed both;
neither bit is wired (`src/pkg_elevate.pdx` notes bits 0x02/0x04 as
originally planned for M4, which closed without them). `list`,
`verify` and `keys` never elevate -- they never mutate `/pkgs`.

pkg NEVER runs with ambient write authority on /pkgs/. Write caps are
acquired per-operation via the elevate broker per D4 discipline. See
caps.decl in the pkg repo for the full manifest.

EXAMPLES

The outputs below are the pinned 1.0.0 behaviour from
tests/m4-003-qemu-smoke/expected/full-matrix.txt -- every mutating
path halts at a substrate seam, so these are exactly what a real
paideia-os user sees today, not an aspirational happy path.

Install a package (refuses at the header stage; no network fetch
exists at 1.0.0, and neither verify seam is reachable yet):
  pkg install libpng
  # -> pkg install: staging manifest for package 'libpng'
  # -> pkg install: header parse failed (see errno)      [stderr]
  # -> exit 1

List installed packages:
  pkg list
  # -> installed packages:
  # ->   (none -- pkg list wires to /system/packages/ readdir at M2)
  # -> exit 0

Remove a package (refuses at the lookup stage; elevate now requested
first per ENH-008, but the broker is unregistered so the request never
dispatches -- see paideia-os R48-PREP-005):
  pkg remove libpng
  # -> pkg remove: removing name 'libpng'
  # -> pkg remove: /system/packages/ readdir unavailable at M2 (R42)  [stderr]
  # -> exit 1

Re-verify an installed package's signatures (stub):
  pkg verify
  # -> pkg verify: body not implemented at M1 (lands at M2)
  # -> exit 3

Unknown or missing subcommand:
  pkg banana
  # -> pkg: unknown subcommand 'banana'                  [stderr]
  # -> exit 2
  pkg
  # -> usage: pkg <install|remove|list|verify|keys> [ARG]  [stderr]
  # -> exit 2

--help / --version (ENH-006 #31), with no subcommand present:
  pkg --version
  # -> pkg 1.0.0
  # -> exit 0

