AUDIT

Every pkg subcommand journals to /system/audit/user-events/
pkg-<ts>-<audit_id>.pdxevent before emitting any output. If the audit
broker is unavailable, the subcommand emits no output of its own and
exits 4 (`AUDIT_EXIT_BROKER_FAIL`, split from `EXIT_NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED`
at ENH-003 #28 -- the two used to share exit code 3). The audit record
shape (libpdx-audit v0.2):

  audit_id      : u64            -- monotonic per-tool counter
  tool          : "pkg"
  subcommand    : "install" | "remove" | "list" | "verify" | "keys"
  argv          : bytes          -- full argv for reconstruction
  user          : Cap<KIND_USER> -- invoker identity
  output_schema : "pdxsig.pkg.pmf.v1" (list) | "pdxsig.pkg.ipr.v1" (install) | empty
  output_hash   : u64             -- low qword of the schema-hash constant
                                     (synthetic at 1.0.0 -- a real BLAKE3/
                                     sha3-256 of the emitted bytes lands
                                     once a consumer needs it; see ENH-012 #37)
  exit_code     : i32
  wall_time_ns  : u64

`list` and `install` populate output_schema/output_hash once per run
(ENH-012 #37); `remove`, `verify` and `keys` emit no schema record at
1.0.0 so the column is empty for those subcommands' audit entries.
`pkg install` additionally journals one InstallProgressRecord per
stage to the semantic pipe (not the audit journal); the audit journal
records the final exit only.

VERSION

pkg 1.0.0 (2026-08-22). See CHANGELOG.md and design/enhancement-plan.md
in the pkg repo for the post-1.0.0 enhancement wave and known
limitations. This file was pinned to source at ENH-002 (#27); it had
drifted to describe a substantially larger tool than the one that
exists (`design/enhancement-plan.md` §2 has the full audit).
